188	      `What was wrong with it:\n${input.problem}\n\n` +
189	      `Proposed replacement:\n${input.replacement}\n\n` +
190	      `Answer "improved" if the replacement fixes the stated problem, keeps the ` +
191	      `passage's meaning and facts, and would read naturally in the draft. ` +
192	      `Answer "not_improved" if it misses the problem, changes the meaning, ` +
193	      `drops facts, or reads worse.`,
194	    IMPROVEMENT,
195	  );
